# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# StonkSmith
#
# Everything above is the stock GitHub Python template and is left untouched so
# that refreshing it stays a clean diff. None of it protects anything this
# project actually writes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The operator's live config. Anchored to the repository root on purpose: it has
# the same *name* as the shipped default at src/stonksmith/etc/stonksmith.conf,
# which is tracked, so a bare `*.conf` would ignore that too and every edit to it
# would need `git add -f`. Theirs carries a SnapTrade client id, a pay grade, a
# service date and two contribution percentages.
/stonksmith.conf
/.stonksmith/

# Account databases: every account number, balance, holding and transaction the
# tool has recorded. `db.sqlite3` in the Django block above is Django's name and
# matches none of ours -- a broker database is <broker>.db under a workspace.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Page captures and screenshots. These are the raw signed-in page, unredacted,
# and docs/live-verification.md tells you to open one and quote it in an issue --
# so nothing should make committing one the easy mistake. The HTML fixtures under
# tests/ are tracked and negated here rather than left for the next person who
# adds one to rediscover with `git add -f`. A screenshot added under docs/ would
# need the same treatment.
*.html
*.png
!tests/*.html

# Playwright traces: a DOM recording of a signed-in session, screenshots and all.
*_trace.zip

# Google OAuth. gspread keeps these under ~/.config/gspread; authorized_user.json
# is a refresh token for the operator's whole Drive, and a copy of one inside a
# public checkout is the worst thing in this file.
authorized_user.json
credentials.json
token.json

# The response logs under ~/.stonksmith/logs are already covered by `*.log` in
# the template above. Left there rather than duplicated here, but worth knowing
# it is deliberate rather than luck.
